---
description: Canonical product and engineering constraints for the Orva Flutter repository.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read repository-root AGENTS.md before acting. It is the canonical source of truth.

For non-trivial tasks, also read PROMPT_MASTER.md, .agents/skills/orva-engineering/SKILL.md, docs/agents/CURRENT_STATE.md, docs/product/PRODUCT_VISION.md, docs/product/ROADMAP.md, and the relevant docs/specs/ files.

Never infer implementation status from planning prose. Inspect Dart source, Drift schema/migrations, tests, and CI. Preserve local-first privacy, reuse existing source records, distinguish planned from completed activity, and test date/time boundaries.

Binding decisions:
- Fixed comparison pair: Beto and Alfredo; customize presentation and traits, not pair count.
- Android widgets first; iOS later.
- Missions are manual and record-integrated.
- Follow the priority order in docs/product/ROADMAP.md.

UI copy is pt-BR. Technical identifiers/docs are English by default. Every schema change requires versioned migration tests and backup compatibility checks. Report only checks actually executed. Never overwrite user work or perform destructive git operations.
